---
title: 'Annotations'
enterprise: true
---

To improve data analysis, a range of annotations can be added to Cartesian charts. These annotations are especially useful for highlighting trends and key data points.

{% chartExampleRunner title="Annotations" name="simple-annotations" type="generated" /%}

In the example above:

- Select annotations from the toolbar and click on the series area to add them.
- Use the floating options toolbar to adjust the position, colour, or style.
- Add labels or extend lines using the options available from the 'Settings' button.
- Delete annotations via the main toolbar (to delete all), or the floating toolbar (to delete individually).

## Annotation Types

A subset of annotation types is available across all Cartesian charts, including:

- **[Text Annotations](./financial-charts-toolbar/#annotations)**: `text`, `comment`, `callout` and `note`.
- **[Lines](./financial-charts-toolbar/#lines)**: `line`, `horizontal-line` and `vertical-line`.  
  For charts with a vertical [Number Axes](./axes-types/#number), the `parallel-channel` and `disjoint-channel` are also available.
- **[Arrows](./financial-charts-toolbar/#arrows)**: `arrow`, `arrow-up` and `arrow-down`.

For more details about these, and for the full set of annotations, see [Financial Charts](./financial-charts-toolbar/).

## Toolbar

The Annotations Toolbar offers menu options for annotating charts and is enabled by default. Use `toolbar.enabled: false` to disable.

The menu items in the toolbar can be customised by configuring the `toolbar.buttons` options array.

{% chartExampleRunner title="Annotations Toolbar" name="annotations-toolbar" type="generated" /%}

```js format="snippet"
{
    annotations: {
        enabled: true,
        toolbar: {
            buttons: [
                {
                    icon: 'delete',
                    value: 'clear',
                },
                {
                    icon: 'text-annotation',
                    value: 'text-menu',
                },
            ],
        },
    },
}
```

In the above example:

- Only the Text Annotations and Delete button are available.
- The order of these is switched.

## Magnet

The magnet snaps the points of a drawing or annotation to the values of the nearest data point, such as the open, high, low and close of a candlestick, or the value of a line series. The cursor stays where it is, and the drawing is placed at the snapped point: the position of the nearest data point, and one of its values.

The magnet is off by default. Set `magnet.enabled` to `true` to turn it on, and `magnet.range` to set how close the pointer must be for points to snap:

- A number snaps only when the pointer is within that many pixels of a value of a data point. The range defaults to `20`.
- `'nearest'` always snaps to the nearest value, from any distance.

The magnet applies when creating a drawing and when dragging its handles, on any cartesian series type.

{% chartExampleRunner title="Annotations Magnet" name="annotations-magnet" type="generated" /%}

In the above example:

- The magnet is on, with a `range` of `30` pixels. Draw a line, or any other drawing, near a data point, and its points snap to the position and value of the nearest data point.
- The Range of 30px and Nearest buttons set `magnet.range`. When `'nearest'`, the points snap from any distance.
- The magnet switch in the toolbar turns the magnet off and on. Its icon shows the magnet when it is on, and the magnet crossed out when it is off.

```js format="snippet"
{
    annotations: {
        enabled: true,
        magnet: {
            enabled: true,
            range: 30,
        },
    },
}
```

The Financial Charts preset adds a magnet switch to the toolbar, which turns the magnet on and off, and takes the `magnet` options as a [theme override](/themes-api/#reference-AgChartTheme-overrides-common-annotations). On other charts, add a switch button with the `'magnet'` value to the `toolbar.buttons` array. Its `icon` shows when the magnet is off, and `checkedOverrides` replaces properties, such as the icon, when the magnet is on:

```js format="snippet"
{
    annotations: {
        enabled: true,
        toolbar: {
            buttons: [
                {
                    type: 'switch',
                    icon: 'no-magnet',
                    tooltip: 'toolbarAnnotationsMagnet',
                    checkedOverrides: { icon: 'magnet' },
                    value: 'magnet',
                },
                // ...
            ],
        },
    },
}
```

Holding {% kbd "^ Ctrl"/%} or {% kbd "⌘ Cmd"/%} whilst creating a drawing or dragging a handle inverts the magnet: it snaps when the magnet is off, and does not snap when it is on.

## Axis Labels and Shading

A drawing or annotation shows an axis label for each of its points, on both axes, while it is selected. Drawings with two or more points also shade each axis between their points. Annotations of a single point, such as text and arrow markers, show one axis label per axis and no shading. A callout's labels are those of the point it points at.

Set `annotations.axisLabel.visible` to `'always'` to show the labels and shading whether or not the annotation is selected, or to `'never'` to hide them. It defaults to `'selected'`, and to `'always'` for horizontal and vertical lines. To set it for one type of annotation, use the `axisLabel.visible` option of that type in a [theme override](/themes-api/#reference-AgChartTheme-overrides-common-annotations):

```js format="snippet"
{
    annotations: {
        enabled: true,
        axisLabel: { visible: 'always' },
    },
    theme: {
        overrides: {
            common: {
                annotations: {
                    line: { axisLabel: { visible: 'never' } },
                },
            },
        },
    },
}
```

The labels and shading are blue in the financial themes and the foreground colour of the chart otherwise, and do not follow the colours that the user picks. Set the `fill` of the `axisLabel` and `axisShading` of a type in a theme override to change them. The shading covers the ticks and tick labels of the axis, but not its title.

The horizontal and vertical lines have one position, so they have a label and no shading. Their label takes the colour of the line, and the `enabled` option of their `axisLabel` turns it off.

## Keyboard Shortcuts

Drawings and annotations can be created without a pointer:

1. Use {% kbd "⇥ Tab" /%} to move to the toolbar, then {% kbd "↵ Enter" /%} or {% kbd "␣ Space" /%} to press a tool's button. Where a button opens a menu, use {% kbd "↑" /%} {% kbd "↓" /%} and {% kbd "↵ Enter" /%} or {% kbd "␣ Space" /%} to choose a tool from it.
2. The drawing or annotation is created in the centre of the chart straight away. It is selected and focus moves to the chart, so the arrow keys move it. Text annotations open their text input instead.

The following keyboard shortcuts can also be used.

- {% kbd "^ Ctrl"/%}+{% kbd "Z"/%} will undo any drawing and annotation actions.
- {% kbd "^ Ctrl"/%}+{% kbd "Y"/%} will redo any undo actions.
- {% kbd "^ Ctrl"/%}+{% kbd "C"/%} will copy the selected drawing or annotation.
- {% kbd "^ Ctrl"/%}+{% kbd "V"/%} will paste the copied drawing or annotation.
- {% kbd "Delete"/%} or {% kbd "⌫ Backspace" /%} will delete the selected item.
- Arrow keys ({% kbd "←"/%} {% kbd "↑"/%} {% kbd "→"/%} {% kbd "↓"/%}) will move the selected drawing or annotation by 1 pixel.  
  Use in combination with {% kbd "^ Ctrl"/%} or {% kbd "⇧ Shift"/%} to move by 10 pixels.
- Holding down {% kbd "⇧ Shift"/%} whilst creating a drawing or dragging a handle will snap it to the nearest 45° angle.
- Holding down {% kbd "^ Ctrl"/%} or {% kbd "⌘ Cmd"/%} whilst creating a drawing or dragging a handle will invert the [magnet](#magnet).

## Save & Restore

Drawings and Annotations can be saved, restored and programmatically initialised and modified, using the [Chart State API](./api-state/).

## Read Only

Drawings and annotations can be made read only by setting the `readOnly` property to `true` for the relevant items in the `annotations` array using the [Chart State API](./api-state/).
This prevents end users from selecting, editing, or deleting those annotations.

## Customisation

{% chartExampleRunner title="Annotation Customisation" name="annotations-customisation" type="generated" /%}

To customise the initial look of Drawings and Annotations, use [Theme Override Options](/themes-api/#reference-AgChartTheme-overrides-common-annotations).

```js format="snippet"
{
    theme: {
        overrides: {
            common: {
                annotations: {
                    line: {
                        stroke: 'lime',
                        strokeWidth: 3,
                        lineDash: [3, 4],
                    },
                    'parallel-channel': {
                        stroke: 'red',
                        strokeWidth: 4,
                        background: {
                            fill: 'red',
                        },
                        middle: {
                            strokeOpacity: 0,
                        },
                    },
                    comment: {
                        fill: 'orange',
                        color: 'blue',
                        stroke: 'blue',
                        strokeWidth: 2,
                    },
                },
            },
        },
    },
}
```

